{"answer":"Amazon states that its business is affected by seasonality, which historically has resulted in higher sales volume during its fourth quarter, which ends December 31 [Source 1][Source 2][Source 3].  

Amazon’s disclosures for its Amazon Web Services segment note that the usage of technology infrastructure assets by the North America and International segments can fluctuate on a quarter‑to‑quarter basis and is affected by seasonality, peak periods, new product or service offerings, and other factors [Source 4][Source 5].  

Accordingly, Amazon attributes its seasonal effects to higher sales in the fourth quarter and to variations in infrastructure usage that occur during peak periods [Source 1][Source 4].","answer_relevancy":1,"citation_completeness":1,"citation_correctness":1,"citation_marker_integrity":1,"faithfulness":1,"refusal_correctness":null}

